not even death could keep picard from  coming back for season two the star trek  universe continues to boldly go where no  show was gone before  sort of as it follows jean-luc picard  years after his adventures on the  starship enterprise  the first season sees a former admiral  investigate the truth behind data's  daughter and a new breed of synthetic  beings his mission takes him across the  universe even revisiting his time with  the borg while also dealing with a  sinister romulan plot there's also the  small problem that picard is dying of  aeromotic syndrome a degenerative  condition that slowly robs him of his  memory it's an action-packed season that  ends as dr agnes jarati transfers  picard's consciousness into a synthetic  body don't worry this doesn't mean he's  immortal the body has been programmed to  expire around the same time picard would  have died naturally so that's good  anyway from there the universe is  picard's oyster since he has the crew of  last serena to go on more adventures  with but picard season 2 will up the  stakes for the show's sophomore season  with the extra dimensional being known  as q returning to break the universe as  one final task for the series namesake  hero  a season throws picard and his crew back  into the 21st century to see how they  save the future if anyone can fix the  fabric of reality it's a former captain  of the enterprise that's for sure but  what do fans need to know about picard  season 2 first things first the good  news is that picard season 2 is heading  to our screens very soon it will arrive  on paramount plus on march 3rd there's a  total of 10 episodes this season so it's  keeping the story quite tight compared  to the 20 plus episode long seasons of  star trek the next generation the second  season will end on may 5th but it's not  going to be the end of picard paramount  worked back to back on season 2 and the  final third season so what does this  mean for the adventure to come well  according to star trek.com q's final  trial will force the la serena crew to  confront the perils of 21st century  earth it seems likely that this threat  will bleed into the third season in some  way considering paramount worked on both  seasons at the same time show runner  terry mutalis told sfx there are some  legendary moments ahead it's worth  noting that although picard season 2  starts airing on march 3rd the third  season doesn't have an official release  date just yet but deadline previously  reported that paramount is aiming for  2023  unsurprisingly patrick stewart is coming  back to play jean-luc picard or should  we say the synthetic version of picard  he'll also be joined by santiago cabrera  who plays cristobal rios the captain of  the la serena allison pill will reprise  her role as dr agnes gerardi although  thankfully her scheming days are over  after her heroic turn midway through the  first season michelle hurd is also  coming back as picard's confidante rafi  massacre while lisa briones will return  his fellow synthetic being soji rounding  out the last serena crew is evan evagora  as warrior monk elnor original next  generation star brent spiner is also set  to return a scientist dr alton in a  gosung voyager star jerry ryan will step  into seven of nine shoes again and orla  brady will continue to appear as lariss  picard's romulan housekeeper but the  guest stars of picard season 2 are  interesting too whoopi goldberg will  play the diplomatic gaining again  offering council to picard when he needs  it most on the villain side of things  john de lancie will cause havoc for the  gang as q and annie worshing will  replace alice krieg as a borg queen  remember picard has dabbled with the  borg in the past he was assimilated into  the hive as the cutest of borg so it  will be interesting to see how the borg  queen reacts to seeing him again after  several decades paramount plus released  a full two minute long look at picard  season 2 on star trek day 2021 the  footage shows jean luke wandering around  his vineyard reminiscing about his  childhood days moderation from q  explains that the trial he subjected  humanity to all the way back in the next  generation season 1 never ended from  there the action really gets going with  rios and the last serena crew realizing  that q has changed the past so that the  world has been transformed into a  totalitarian nightmare it's a far cry  away from the idealized future of star  fleet and the federation that's for sure  the crew already knows that time's been  altered because seven of nine instantly  realizes that she has no borg parts on  her face anymore clearly the fascist  regime cut the borg off at the knees the  gang meets up with the bald queen using  her technology to teleport to the past  in an attempt to fix whatever q did to  the timeline it's not exactly a new idea  kirk and the original enterprise crew  travel to the 20th century in star trek  iv the voyage home but hopefully the  writers of picard find inventive ways of  pushing these characters further than  the typical fish out of water comedy  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one
 

